From: Pontus Oldberg <pontus.oldberg@invector.se>
Date: 2026-08-31
Subject: [PATCH] ElectricalEnergyMeasurement: size the measurement table by
 instances, not by the endpoint space

gMeasurements is indexed by emberAfGetClusterServerEndpointIndex(), whose
range on a build with dynamic endpoints is the whole dynamic endpoint space.
The array is therefore declared as

    MeasurementData gMeasurements[MATTER_DM_..._SERVER_ENDPOINT_COUNT +
                                  CHIP_DEVICE_CONFIG_DYNAMIC_ENDPOINT_COUNT];

and is charged in full the moment the cluster enters the build, whether or
not any endpoint ever carries it. sizeof(MeasurementData) is 496 bytes on
32-bit ARM, so a bridge with CHIP_DEVICE_CONFIG_DYNAMIC_ENDPOINT_COUNT of 16
reserves 8,432 bytes of RAM for a cluster a given composition may never
declare. On a part with 256 KB that is 3.2% of the whole address space held
against a possibility.

Cap the table at the number of endpoints that can carry measurements at once
instead, and claim slots by endpoint id:

  CHIP_CONFIG_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_MAX_INSTANCES sets the length.
  Its DEFAULT IS THE OLD EXPRESSION, so a platform that does not set it gets
  today's array, today's size and today's behaviour, byte for byte. Only a
  platform that opts in pays the lookup and saves the RAM.

  MeasurementDataForEndpoint() keeps its existing validity gate unchanged
  (emberAfGetClusterServerEndpointIndex() != kEmberInvalidEndpointIndex is
  what rejects an endpoint that is unconfigured, disabled, or does not carry
  this cluster server), then searches the claim table for the endpoint and
  claims a free slot on first use. Every caller reaches the data through
  this one function, so no call site changes.

  IT THEREFORE MUTATES, which the comment above it now says plainly. Read
  behaviour is preserved exactly, and that rests on the gate: an endpoint
  that does not carry the cluster server can never claim, so every claimant
  is one that would have claimed at its first write anyway, and a read of a
  live but never-written endpoint still returns a value-initialised slot
  rather than nullptr. Under exhaustion, WHICH endpoints hold slots depends
  on which is touched first, so an application that does not call
  SetMeasurementAccuracy() at startup gets its slot order from whichever
  endpoint a controller happens to read first. That is a fair design, and it
  is a change a reviewer should see stated rather than have to infer.

  A dynamic endpoint can be taken down, and nothing tells this file when.
  Rather than add a release entry point that every bridge would have to
  learn to call, a claim whose endpoint no longer serves the cluster is
  treated as free and reused. The reclaim is therefore automatic and the
  cluster's API is unchanged.

  Exhaustion returns nullptr, which every caller in this file already
  handles: reads encode null or CHIP_ERROR_NOT_FOUND, writes return
  CHIP_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT. The log line names the macro to raise. A
  platform that must not present an endpoint it cannot serve should ALSO
  bound the count on its own side, before the endpoint is built, because
  this file learns about the endpoint too late to refuse it: by the time
  SetMeasurementAccuracy() fails, the endpoint is live and a controller can
  already read the mandatory Accuracy attribute it can no longer serve.

The replaced "index >= MATTER_ARRAY_SIZE(gMeasurements)" guard becomes
unnecessary: the returned pointer is now always into the pool, and the
bound is enforced by the claim rather than by an index range check.

Cost on the read path: the claim walks the pool at most twice and can call
emberAfGetClusterServerEndpointIndex() up to MAX_INSTANCES times when the
pool is full. Bounded by a small constant and paid only on the first touch
of an endpoint, but it is a getter that now does ember lookups.

Behaviour is identical for any composition with no more than
CHIP_CONFIG_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_MAX_INSTANCES endpoints carrying
the cluster, which for the default value is every composition the old code
could serve at all.

One line is downstream-only and marked as such in place:
HEARTH_EEM_POOL_PATCH_REV lets a build system tell a tree carrying this
revision of the patch from one carrying an older revision, which a search
for the configuration macro cannot. Drop it when upstreaming.

Measured on nRF54L15 with the macro set to 8: gMeasurements 8,432 to 3,968
bytes, plus 24 bytes of claim table, 4,440 bytes of .bss reclaimed.
---
 .../ElectricalEnergyMeasurementCluster.cpp    | 111 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 99 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

--- a/src/app/clusters/electrical-energy-measurement-server/ElectricalEnergyMeasurementCluster.cpp
+++ b/src/app/clusters/electrical-energy-measurement-server/ElectricalEnergyMeasurementCluster.cpp
@@ -39,8 +39,53 @@
 using namespace chip::app::Clusters::ElectricalEnergyMeasurement::Attributes;
 using namespace chip::app::Clusters::ElectricalEnergyMeasurement::Structs;

-MeasurementData gMeasurements[MATTER_DM_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_CLUSTER_SERVER_ENDPOINT_COUNT +
-                              CHIP_DEVICE_CONFIG_DYNAMIC_ENDPOINT_COUNT];
+/*
+ * The measurement table used to be indexed directly by the cluster server
+ * endpoint index, which on a build with dynamic endpoints spans every dynamic
+ * slot whether or not the endpoint occupying it carries this cluster. Sizing
+ * the table that way charges sizeof(MeasurementData) * (fixed + dynamic) to
+ * every build that merely compiles the cluster in, including one that never
+ * declares an energy endpoint at all. On a constrained bridge that is several
+ * kilobytes of RAM held for endpoints which do not exist.
+ *
+ * CHIP_CONFIG_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_MAX_INSTANCES caps the table at the
+ * number of endpoints that can carry measurements AT ONCE. A slot is claimed by
+ * endpoint id the first time that endpoint's data is asked for and found by id
+ * afterwards, so the table no longer has to be as long as the endpoint space.
+ *
+ * The default is the old size, so a platform that does not set the macro keeps
+ * today's behaviour exactly, table length included.
+ */
+#ifndef CHIP_CONFIG_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_MAX_INSTANCES
+#define CHIP_CONFIG_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_MAX_INSTANCES                                                                    \
+    (MATTER_DM_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_CLUSTER_SERVER_ENDPOINT_COUNT + CHIP_DEVICE_CONFIG_DYNAMIC_ENDPOINT_COUNT)
+#endif
+
+// Downstream marker, not part of the change being proposed: it lets a build
+// system tell a tree carrying THIS revision of the patch from one carrying an
+// older revision, which a search for the macro above cannot. Drop this line
+// when upstreaming.
+#define HEARTH_EEM_POOL_PATCH_REV 2
+
+MeasurementData gMeasurements[CHIP_CONFIG_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_MAX_INSTANCES];
+
+namespace {
+
+// Which endpoint owns each slot of gMeasurements. The "used" flag is a separate
+// array rather than a kInvalidEndpointId sentinel so that neither array needs a
+// static initialiser.
+EndpointId gMeasurementSlotEndpoint[CHIP_CONFIG_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_MAX_INSTANCES];
+bool gMeasurementSlotUsed[CHIP_CONFIG_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_MAX_INSTANCES];
+
+// True when endpointId is configured, enabled, and carries this cluster server.
+bool IsLiveMeasurementEndpoint(EndpointId endpointId)
+{
+    return emberAfGetClusterServerEndpointIndex(endpointId, app::Clusters::ElectricalEnergyMeasurement::Id,
+                                                MATTER_DM_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_CLUSTER_SERVER_ENDPOINT_COUNT) !=
+        kEmberInvalidEndpointIndex;
+}
+
+} // namespace

 CHIP_ERROR ElectricalEnergyMeasurementAttrAccess::Init()
 {
@@ -144,22 +189,68 @@
     return mOptionalAttrs.Has(aOptionalAttrs);
 }

+// NOTE: this function MUTATES. It claims a pool slot for endpointId on first
+// use, so it is no longer a pure lookup even though its signature is unchanged
+// and every existing caller is unaffected.
+//
+// Read behaviour is preserved exactly, and that rests on the gate below: an
+// endpoint that does not carry this cluster server can never claim, so every
+// claimant is an endpoint that would have claimed at its first write anyway,
+// and a read of a live endpoint that was never written still returns a
+// value-initialised slot rather than nullptr. Under exhaustion, though, WHICH
+// endpoints get slots depends on which is touched first, so an application that
+// does not call SetMeasurementAccuracy() at startup has its slot order decided
+// by whichever endpoint a controller happens to read first.
+//
+// The claim walks the pool at most twice and can call
+// emberAfGetClusterServerEndpointIndex() up to MAX_INSTANCES times when the
+// pool is full. Bounded by a small constant, and only on the first touch of an
+// endpoint, but it is a getter that now does ember lookups and a reader should
+// know that.
 MeasurementData * MeasurementDataForEndpoint(EndpointId endpointId)
 {
-    auto index = emberAfGetClusterServerEndpointIndex(endpointId, app::Clusters::ElectricalEnergyMeasurement::Id,
-                                                      MATTER_DM_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_CLUSTER_SERVER_ENDPOINT_COUNT);
-
-    if (index == kEmberInvalidEndpointIndex)
+    // Unchanged gate: an endpoint that is not configured, not enabled, or does
+    // not carry this cluster server has no measurement data and claims no slot.
+    if (!IsLiveMeasurementEndpoint(endpointId))
     {
         return nullptr;
     }

-    if (index >= MATTER_ARRAY_SIZE(gMeasurements))
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < MATTER_ARRAY_SIZE(gMeasurements); i++)
+    {
+        if (gMeasurementSlotUsed[i] && gMeasurementSlotEndpoint[i] == endpointId)
+        {
+            return &gMeasurements[i];
+        }
+    }
+
+    size_t slot = MATTER_ARRAY_SIZE(gMeasurements);
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < MATTER_ARRAY_SIZE(gMeasurements); i++)
     {
-        ChipLogError(NotSpecified, "Internal error: invalid/unexpected energy measurement index.");
+        // A free slot, or one whose endpoint has since been taken down: nothing
+        // tells this file when a dynamic endpoint goes away, so a stale claim is
+        // recognised by asking whether its endpoint still serves this cluster.
+        if (!gMeasurementSlotUsed[i] || !IsLiveMeasurementEndpoint(gMeasurementSlotEndpoint[i]))
+        {
+            slot = i;
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+
+    if (slot == MATTER_ARRAY_SIZE(gMeasurements))
+    {
+        ChipLogError(NotSpecified,
+                     "Electrical Energy Measurement: no measurement slot free for endpoint %u; raise "
+                     "CHIP_CONFIG_ELECTRICAL_ENERGY_MEASUREMENT_MAX_INSTANCES (currently %u).",
+                     static_cast<unsigned>(endpointId),
+                     static_cast<unsigned>(MATTER_ARRAY_SIZE(gMeasurements)));
         return nullptr;
     }
-    return &gMeasurements[index];
+
+    gMeasurements[slot]            = MeasurementData();
+    gMeasurementSlotEndpoint[slot] = endpointId;
+    gMeasurementSlotUsed[slot]     = true;
+    return &gMeasurements[slot];
 }

 CHIP_ERROR SetMeasurementAccuracy(EndpointId endpointId, const MeasurementAccuracyStruct::Type & accuracy)
